 ## Overview
-Hierarchical sampling is a two-stage strategy for volume rendering that improves image quality by concentrating samples in regions of high geometric or color complexity, addressing the bottleneck of point sampling in neural radiance fields [S2, S3, unofficial]. It sets itself apart from uniform sampling by using a coarse network to estimate density and guide importance sampling for a fine network [S6].
